@host = http://localhost:3000

### ── Fill these in as you go ──────────────────────────────
@foodId = 11634
@servingId = 135302
@otherFoodId = 7097
@otherServingId = 122315
@entryId = 1
@today = 2026-09-10

### ── Identities ───────────────────────────────────────────

### Login as A
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### Login as B
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@outlook.com", "password": "administrator" }

### ── Discovery: get ids ───────────────────────────────────

### Search a food  → set @foodId
GET {{host}}/api/foods/search?q=banana&limit=5

### Its servings   → set @servingId
GET {{host}}/api/foods/{{foodId}}

### A different food → set @otherFoodId, @otherServingId
GET {{host}}/api/foods/search?q=chicken%20breast&limit=5

###
GET {{host}}/api/foods/{{otherFoodId}}

### ── Happy path (as A) ────────────────────────────────────

### 1. Create with a serving → 201, set @entryId from the response
POST {{host}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "foodId": {{foodId}},
  "servingId": {{servingId}},
  "quantity": 1.5,
  "mealType": "BREAKFAST",
  "loggedOn": "{{today}}"
}

### 2. Create grams-only (servingId omitted) → 201, serving: null
POST {{host}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "foodId": {{foodId}},
  "quantity": 100,
  "mealType": "LUNCH",
  "loggedOn": "{{today}}"
}

### 3. Patch quantity only → 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/entries/{{entryId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 2 }

### 4. Patch meal type only → 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/entries/{{entryId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mealType": "DINNER" }

### 5. Clear the serving → 200, serving null, quantity now grams
PATCH {{host}}/api/entries/{{entryId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "servingId": null, "quantity": 1.5 }

### ── Ownership (run the B login above first) ──────────────

### 6. B patches A's entry → 403
PATCH {{host}}/api/entries/{{entryId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 999 }

### 7. B deletes A's entry → 403
DELETE {{host}}/api/entries/{{entryId}}

### ── Validation (log back in as A) ────────────────────────

### 8. Empty patch → 400
PATCH {{host}}/api/entries/{{entryId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 9. Typo'd key → 400, not a silent 200
PATCH {{host}}/api/entries/{{entryId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantitiy": 5 }

### 10. Unknown key on create → 400
POST {{host}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "foodId": {{foodId}},
  "quantity": 1,
  "mealType": "BREAKFAST",
  "loggedOn": "{{today}}",
  "calories": 500
}

### 11. Malformed id → 400
PATCH {{host}}/api/entries/abc
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 2 }

### 12. Absent id → 404
DELETE {{host}}/api/entries/99999999

### 13. Impossible date → 400
POST {{host}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "foodId": {{foodId}},
  "quantity": 1,
  "mealType": "BREAKFAST",
  "loggedOn": "2026-02-31"
}

### 14. Date with a time component → 400
POST {{host}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "foodId": {{foodId}},
  "quantity": 1,
  "mealType": "BREAKFAST",
  "loggedOn": "2026-09-08T00:00:00.000Z"
}

### 15. Bad meal type → 400
POST {{host}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "foodId": {{foodId}},
  "quantity": 1,
  "mealType": "BRUNCH",
  "loggedOn": "{{today}}"
}

### 16. Negative quantity → 400
POST {{host}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "foodId": {{foodId}},
  "quantity": -1,
  "mealType": "BREAKFAST",
  "loggedOn": "{{today}}"
}

### ── Cross-resource coherence ─────────────────────────────

### 17. Serving from a different food → 400
POST {{host}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "foodId": {{foodId}},
  "servingId": {{otherServingId}},
  "quantity": 1,
  "mealType": "BREAKFAST",
  "loggedOn": "{{today}}"
}

### 18. Nonexistent food → 404
POST {{host}}/api/entries
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "foodId": 99999999,
  "quantity": 1,
  "mealType": "BREAKFAST",
  "loggedOn":
}

### List a populated day
GET {{host}}/api/entries?date=2026-09-08
Content-Type: application/json

### List an empty day
GET {{host}}/api/entries?date=2020-01-01
Content-Type: application/json

### Invalid date — rolls to March 3rd, must 400
GET {{host}}/api/entries?date=2026-02-31
Content-Type: application/json

### Typo'd param — .strict(), must 400
GET {{host}}/api/entries?dat=2026-09-08
Content-Type: application/json

### B lists A's populated day — must be empty, not 403
GET {{host}}/api/entries?date=2026-09-08